{"title":"2021 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 4","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><dl><dd><i>The following problem is from the <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_7\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"2021 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 7\">2021 AMC 10A #7</a> and <a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">2021 AMC 12A #4</a>, so those problems redirect to this page.</i></dd></dl>\n<div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution_1_(Comprehensive_Explanation_of_Logic)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1 (Comprehensive Explanation of Logic)</span></a>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_1.1_(Intuitive)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2.1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1.1 (Intuitive)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Solution_1.2_(Rigorous)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2.2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1.2 (Rigorous)</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#Solution_2_(Process_of_Elimination)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2 (Process of Elimination)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-6\"><a href=\"#Solution_3_(Rigorous)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 3 (Rigorous)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-7\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_(Simple_&amp;_Quick)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution (Simple &amp; Quick)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-8\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_by_Hawk_Math\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">6</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution by Hawk Math</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-9\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_by_OmegaLearn_(Using_Logic_to_Eliminate_Choices)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">7</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution by OmegaLearn (Using Logic to Eliminate Choices)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-10\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">8</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-11\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_by_TheBeautyofMath\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">9</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution by TheBeautyofMath</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-12\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_by_The_Learning_Royal\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">10</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution by The Learning Royal</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-13\"><a href=\"#See_also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">11</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_4&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Tom has a collection of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/3/0/030e19e4e2f1c074127cb50581e8496470c5419f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$13$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> snakes, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/c/c7cab1a05e1e0c1d51a6a219d96577a16b7abf9d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> of which are purple and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/9/0/79069377f91364c2f87a64e5f9f562a091c8a6c1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> of which are happy. He observes that\n</p>\n<ul><li>all of his happy snakes can add,</li></ul>\n<ul><li>none of his purple snakes can subtract, and</li></ul>\n<ul><li>all of his snakes that can't subtract also can't add.</li></ul>\n<p>Which of these conclusions can be drawn about Tom's snakes?\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/8/7/e8738bbc91069d2db6a97b6ab9b1e13052ac4606.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A) }$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"28\" height=\"17\" /> Purple snakes can add.\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/0/6/506e909041d36bd739c8c959d341fcfbba3e9ad7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(B) }$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"27\" height=\"17\" /> Purple snakes are happy.\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/a/b/0ab3a9c13a5c376b1660f46d00b9007dbae240cb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(C) }$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"27\" height=\"17\" /> Snakes that can add are purple.\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/7/8/3787f1b7ce783a57c3a0d02ca4d485ccc950ff0a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(D) }$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"28\" height=\"17\" /> Happy snakes are not purple.\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/d/81d05263c2e18459105296c8e3e06c9fddddb735.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(E) }$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"26\" height=\"17\" /> Happy snakes can't subtract.\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_1_.28Comprehensive_Explanation_of_Logic.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1_(Comprehensive_Explanation_of_Logic)\">Solution 1 (Comprehensive Explanation of Logic)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_4&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1 (Comprehensive Explanation of Logic)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>We are given that\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/d/6/ad6f2ea2312d70b267a9e7b4814601e451acf567.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\begin{align*} \\text{happy}&amp;\\Longrightarrow\\text{can add}, &amp;(1) \\\\ \\text{purple}&amp;\\Longrightarrow\\text{cannot subtract}, \\hspace{15mm} &amp;(2) \\\\ \\text{cannot subtract}&amp;\\Longrightarrow\\text{cannot add}. &amp;(3) \\end{align*}\" width=\"422\" height=\"68\" />\nTwo solutions follow from here:\n</p>\n<h3><span id=\"Solution_1.1_.28Intuitive.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1.1_(Intuitive)\">Solution 1.1 (Intuitive)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_4&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1.1 (Intuitive)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>Combining <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/2/f/62f62a19f0425d8e6121ca0c1cfd3ce96e43c9c5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(2)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"21\" height=\"18\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/8/8/b88ea3916e8089c7edbccc3ff91e58e01a6e2682.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(3)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"21\" height=\"18\" /> gives\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/5/c/b5c1e63e79b4a896e717c54be6aa16453db27892.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\begin{align*} \\text{happy}&amp;\\Longrightarrow\\text{can add}, &amp;(1) \\\\ \\lefteqn{\\underbrace{\\phantom{\\text{purple}\\Longrightarrow\\text{cannot subtract}}}_{(2)}}\\text{purple}&amp;\\Longrightarrow\\overbrace{\\text{cannot subtract}\\Longrightarrow\\text{cannot add}}^{(3)}. \\hspace{2.5mm} &amp;(*) \\end{align*}\" width=\"401\" height=\"94\" />\nClearly, the answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/a/a/3aaffab0f4c5610b12f5f960dbaabe4db56f9fe3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{(D)}}.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -10px\" width=\"44\" height=\"28\" />\n</p><p>~MRENTHUSIASM (credit given to abhinavg0627)\n</p>\n<h3><span id=\"Solution_1.2_.28Rigorous.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1.2_(Rigorous)\">Solution 1.2 (Rigorous)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_4&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1.2 (Rigorous)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p><i><b>Recall that every conditional statement <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/3/4/4348d2b615a824823c79bdf05c03d2c8af90474d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boldsymbol{p\\Longrightarrow q}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"66\" height=\"13\" /> is always logically equivalent to its contrapositive <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/b/2/8b25dd330aa466dd770b7028e5ff6a764da9ea61.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boldsymbol{\\lnot q\\Longrightarrow\\lnot p.}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"99\" height=\"13\" /></b></i>\n</p><p>Combining <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/2/2626e4d23e233b53c54cc825aae23ebf324ec210.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(1),(2)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"53\" height=\"18\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/8/8/b88ea3916e8089c7edbccc3ff91e58e01a6e2682.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(3)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"21\" height=\"18\" /> gives <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/8/0/2802e3a164d1bd3928538bc149ccf52669d8bf7b.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\lefteqn{\\underbrace{\\phantom{\\text{purple}\\Longrightarrow\\text{cannot subtract}}}_{(2)}}\\text{purple}\\Longrightarrow\\overbrace{\\text{cannot subtract}\\Longrightarrow\\lefteqn{\\underbrace{\\phantom{\\text{cannot add}\\Longrightarrow\\text{not happy}}}_{\\text{Contrapositive of }(1)}}\\text{cannot add}}^{(3)}\\Longrightarrow\\text{not happy}. \\hspace{15mm}(**)\\]\" width=\"540\" height=\"66\" /> Applying the hypothetical syllogism to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/d/f/3df751b6e49a4628ae524db3df528d0d238cf65e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(**),$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"36\" height=\"18\" /> we conclude that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/b/6/fb643faeb7b9041a9516631320bf933c072eb794.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\text{purple}\\Longrightarrow\\text{not happy},\\]\" width=\"163\" height=\"15\" /> whose contrapositive is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/6/7/667d11a0b37ef726db22d335f6439e18b4787550.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\text{happy}\\Longrightarrow\\text{not purple}.\\]\" width=\"162\" height=\"15\" /> Therefore, the answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/a/a/3aaffab0f4c5610b12f5f960dbaabe4db56f9fe3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{(D)}}.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -10px\" width=\"44\" height=\"28\" />\n</p><p><u><b>Remark</b></u>\n</p><p>The conclusions in the other choices do not follow from <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/7/b/87bb5b7b87e36255336a4d58ad014088e83f9358.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(**):$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"41\" height=\"18\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/3/0/c30d3f1a6332d4fb770bf6c3979c136f15169417.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A) }\\text{purple}\\Longrightarrow\\text{can add}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"178\" height=\"17\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/5/2/d52867a51d1c1ea1ae56ef8e506f4d648690e246.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(B) }\\text{purple}\\Longrightarrow\\text{happy}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"164\" height=\"17\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/9/6/596f2da284a5151fb4a23626c6d194afc3d6bab4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(C) }\\text{can add}\\Longrightarrow\\text{purple}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"177\" height=\"17\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/f/1/bf1a9a996607ca32d5b775369b74489360afe766.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(E) }\\text{happy}\\Longrightarrow\\text{cannot subtract}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"231\" height=\"17\" />\n</p><p>~MRENTHUSIASM\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_2_.28Process_of_Elimination.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2_(Process_of_Elimination)\">Solution 2 (Process of Elimination)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_4&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2 (Process of Elimination)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>From Solution 1.1, we can also see this through the process of elimination. \nStatement <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/9/019e9892786e493964e145e7c5cf7b700314e53b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" /> is false because purple snakes cannot add. <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/f/5/ff5fb3d775862e2123b007eb4373ff6cc1a34d4e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" /> is false as well  because since happy snakes can add and purple snakes can not add, purple snakes are not happy snakes. <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/a/2/fa2fa899f0afb05d6837885523503a2d4df434f9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$E$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> is false using the same reasoning, purple snakes are not happy snakes so happy snakes can subtract since purple snakes cannot subtract. <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/3/3/c3355896da590fc491a10150a50416687626d7cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$C$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> is false since snakes that can add are happy, not purple. That leaves statement D. <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/9/3/693c4044f8526a8179956e8ac7a3f2f9d61e2c1c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{(D)}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"43\" height=\"30\" /> is the only correct statement.\n</p><p>~Bakedpotato66\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_3_.28Rigorous.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_3_(Rigorous)\">Solution 3 (Rigorous)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_4&amp;action=edit&amp;section=6\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 3 (Rigorous)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>We first convert each statement to \"If X, then Y\" form:\n</p>\n<ul><li>If a snake is happy, then it can add.</li></ul>\n<ul><li>If a snake is purple, then it can't subtract.</li></ul>\n<ul><li>If a snake can't subtract, then it can't add.</li></ul>\n<p>Now, we simply check the truth value for each statement: \n</p>\n<ol style=\"margin-left: 1.5em;\" type=\"A\">\n  <li>Combining the last two propositions, we have\n<ul><li>If a snake is purple, then it can't add. <p class=\"mw-empty-elt\"></p></li></ul>\nThus, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/4/6/a46f6af01fcf3bb5f6cac2316bc4de9bb3906bec.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A)}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"31\" height=\"18\" /> is never true.</li><p class=\"mw-empty-elt\">\n  </p><li>From the last part, we found that\n<ul><li>If a snake is purple, then it can't add. <p class=\"mw-empty-elt\"></p></li></ul>\nAlso, since the contrapositive of a proposition has the same truth value as the proposition itself, we know, from the first statement, that \n<ul><li>If a snake can't add, then it isn't happy. <p class=\"mw-empty-elt\"></p></li></ul>\nCombining these two propositions, we find that \n<ul><li>If a snake is purple, then it isn't happy. Purple snakes are not happy.</li><p class=\"mw-empty-elt\"></p></ul>\nThus, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/7/1/b7193f66028e13f331d53ff5e6942c4b05587465.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(B)}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"30\" height=\"18\" /> is never true.</li><p class=\"mw-empty-elt\">\n  </p><li>From part <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/b/3/cb3db983b534373488fba3fdfaf7b692194bb301.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A)},$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"33\" height=\"17\" /> we found that \"If a snake is purple, then it can't add.\" This implies its contrapositive, \"If a snake can add, then it is not purple.\" is true, meaning <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/6/9/169b8d69bd74a91e72ec43123070d770633a340a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(C)}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"30\" height=\"18\" /> is NEVER true. [Thanks again to MRENTHUSIASM for pointing this out!]</li><p class=\"mw-empty-elt\">\n  </p><li>From the first statement, we have \n<ul><li>If a snake is happy, then it can add.<p class=\"mw-empty-elt\"></p></li></ul>\nFrom the contrapositive of the third statement, we have\n<ul><li>If a snake can add, then it can subtract. <p class=\"mw-empty-elt\"></p></li></ul>\nThen, from the contrapositive of the second statement, we have \n<ul><li>If a snake can subtract, then it is not purple. <p class=\"mw-empty-elt\"></p></li></ul>\nCombining all of these yields \n<ul><li>If a snake is happy, then it is not purple.<p class=\"mw-empty-elt\"></p></li></ul>\nThus, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/3/0/b305929a95b53f14a0ad53eba1d8560626e1f28b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(D)}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"31\" height=\"18\" /> is always true.</li><p class=\"mw-empty-elt\">\n  </p><li>From the first proposition, we have \n<ul><li>If a snake is happy, then it can add. <p class=\"mw-empty-elt\"></p></li></ul>\nFrom the contrapositive of the third proposition, we have \n<ul><li>If a snake can add, then it can subtract. <p class=\"mw-empty-elt\"></p></li></ul>\nCombining these two propositions gives \n<ul><li>If a snake is happy, then it can subtract. <p class=\"mw-empty-elt\"></p></li></ul>\nThus, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/5/e/75e41e3cd48cee2c6866cfbb4386a8e99d3482f5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(E)}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"29\" height=\"18\" /> is never true.</li><p class=\"mw-empty-elt\">\n</p></ol>\n<p>Therefore, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/9/3/693c4044f8526a8179956e8ac7a3f2f9d61e2c1c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{(D)}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"43\" height=\"30\" /> is our answer.\n</p><p>~ Peace09 (My First Wiki Solution!)\n</p><p>~ MRENTHUSIASM (Revision Suggestions and Code Adjustments)\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Video_Solution_.28Simple_.26_Quick.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_(Simple_&amp;_Quick)\">Video Solution (Simple &amp; Quick)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_4&amp;action=edit&amp;section=7\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution (Simple &amp; Quick)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/hJKHaIcyIxA\">https://youtu.be/hJKHaIcyIxA</a>\n</p><p>~ Education the Study of Everything\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_by_Hawk_Math\">Video Solution by Hawk Math</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_4&amp;action=edit&amp;section=8\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution by Hawk Math\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=P5al76DxyHY\">https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=P5al76DxyHY</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Video_Solution_by_OmegaLearn_.28Using_Logic_to_Eliminate_Choices.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_by_OmegaLearn_(Using_Logic_to_Eliminate_Choices)\">Video Solution by OmegaLearn (Using Logic to Eliminate Choices)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_4&amp;action=edit&amp;section=9\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution by OmegaLearn (Using Logic to Eliminate Choices)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/Mofw3VXHPyg\">https://youtu.be/Mofw3VXHPyg</a>\n</p><p>~ pi_is_3.14\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution\">Video Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_4&amp;action=edit&amp;section=10\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/uDJv06-cNrI\">https://youtu.be/uDJv06-cNrI</a>\n</p><p>~savannahsolver\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_by_TheBeautyofMath\">Video Solution by TheBeautyofMath</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_4&amp;action=edit&amp;section=11\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution by TheBeautyofMath\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/s6E4E06XhPU?t=202\">https://youtu.be/s6E4E06XhPU?t=202</a> (AMC10A)\n</p><p><a